Revised Jan 27, 2018
Accepted Feb 26, 2018
An inclination towards renewable energy resources has been increased due to
the requirement of clean environment and to satisfy the increasing power
demand for the long run. A grid connected system requires the availability of
a transformer in its power conversion stages that provides galvanic isolation
between the grid and the power system. But inclusion of transformer results
in making the system bulky and more expensive. In this paper different
transformer-less PV inverter topologies are analyzed by comparing their
efficiency, leakage current and THD of load current using
MATLAB/Simulink environment. To achieve maximum power from PV
system, maximum power point controller (P&amp;O algorithm) is used. From the
simulation results, modified HB-ZVR is found to have minimum leakage
current and constant common mode voltage with higher efficiency. The
hardware results are obtained for modified HB-ZVR topology.
Keyword:
PV array
MPPT controller
Leakage current
Transformer-less topologies
